# 1Password env-file template — `op run --env-file=.env.op -- <cmd>` resolves
# the op:// references to actual secret values and injects them as env vars
# for the wrapped command. The values never appear in shell scrollback,
# history, or the terminal session of the agent invoking `op run`.
#
# This file is committed (it contains references, not secrets). Anyone with
# read access to the Goldberry Grove - Admin vault's Grove Infra item gets the
# values; anyone without it gets `op` errors and nothing leaks.
#
# Consumed by `make qa-l3-plan` / `make qa-l3-up` and scripts/qa-l3-teardown.sh.
# Those were Infisical's last local-ops consumers; they now read from here
# (GOL-418, closing out the GOL-231 teardown).
#
# Refs are by item UUID + field id rather than name/label, so a rename cannot
# break resolution (GOL-394). EXCEPTION: cf_zone_api_key (TF_VAR_cloudflare_api_token)
# is referenced by item-UUID + field LABEL. Its field was deleted and recreated
# during the GOL-1643 token audit (2026-08-24); a field-uuid ref rots on delete/
# recreate, so the label ref is the resilient choice for a field with that history.
#
# NOT here, deliberately:
#   - GROVE_BRAND_PR_TOKEN — not minted yet (GOL-293). An op:// ref to a
#     missing field is a hard `op run` failure, so it stays an optional
#     shell passthrough; the TF var defaults to "".
#
# Prerequisites in 1Password (Goldberry Grove - Admin → Grove Infra,
# item qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4):
#   - grove_tfstate_access_key_id / grove_tfstate_secret_key (concealed)
#       Spaces key for the grove-tf-state bucket; feeds the TF S3 backend via
#       AWS_*. Scoped on purpose — the broader spaces_bootstrap_* pair
#       (All Buckets / Full Access) is bucket-lifecycle plumbing for the
#       state-backend env and is deliberately NOT used here. Infisical's
#       SPACES_* held the bootstrap pair; this is the least-privilege swap
#       (verified: `terraform init` against this backend succeeds).
#   - do_token                        (concealed) — droplet/domain/ssh-key/
#                                       firewall/database/app scopes
#   - cf_zone_api_key                 (concealed) — user-owned CF token
#                                       (id a27b1709...) that lists all four
#                                       Grove zones + reads DNS records — the
#                                       exact refresh ops this env performs
#                                       (data.cloudflare_zone.apex + the qa_ns
#                                       records on gatheringatthegrove.com).
#                                       Replaces the prior cloudflare_zone_edit_token
#                                       field, which held a REVOKED token and was
#                                       deleted from the item (GOL-1643, token
#                                       audit 2026-08-24). Referenced BY LABEL,
#                                       not field-uuid: uuid refs rot when a field
#                                       is deleted/recreated (the old ref was
#                                       doubly dead — dead value AND dead uuid).
#                                       If a later apply 403s on a record WRITE,
#                                       the token needs DNS:Edit added in the CF
#                                       dashboard (Josh owns the token, can edit
#                                       its policy).
#   - grove_revalidate_secret         (concealed) — hub/tenant ISR revalidation
#   - grove_assets_access_key_id / grove_assets_secret_key /
#     grove_assets_optimize_token     (concealed) — hub assets-ingest
#                                       endpoints (GOL-290/GOL-293)
#   - odoo_api_keys_tf_json           (concealed) — JSON map of per-tenant Odoo
#                                       API keys {goldberry,ggg,nursery}. A TF
#                                       *input* (keys minted in Odoo by a human),
#                                       distinct from the Otto ODOO_API_KEY that
#                                       CI mints and writes back to the
#                                       `Grove CI Writeback` vault (GOL-237).
#                                       Different lifecycle → different home;
#                                       see that vault's runbook for why it
#                                       holds only CI-minted keys.

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/pv3orzpohmz5wtze3gedjg67ma"
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/xvzkhcsyj5sbxmilu5udx4v6la"
TF_VAR_do_token="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/rlnkse5k3p34nwamap5qhquxom"
TF_VAR_cloudflare_api_token="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/cf_zone_api_key"
TF_VAR_grove_revalidate_secret="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/gke7o4aqyljfdo32yy4ayhq474"
TF_VAR_grove_assets_access_key_id="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/tdqeefk4koldmhar6se3crrike"
TF_VAR_grove_assets_secret_key="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/cferjfmpg5fpiucaef2imoah6i"
TF_VAR_grove_assets_optimize_token="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/5yoqp5gx77ijhaegp54ljqjbta"
TF_VAR_odoo_api_keys="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/wxm2iqnkfkvoy2gpwcj2v46wv4"

# --- Stripe sandbox keys (EOM-July QA) --------------------------------------
# Vault `Grove QA`, one item per tenant, field `secret_key` (rk_test_,
# scope-verified 2026-07-20 by qa-tools/check_stripe_key_scopes.py).
# UUID+field-id refs per GOL-394. These are the PER-TENANT App Platform
# storefront keys (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY on digitalocean_app.tenant); distinct
# from the singular stripe_test_* below, which is the Odoo backend key.
TF_VAR_stripe_secret_key_goldberry="op://Grove QA/34vvkjpyiyuq7nyq7rtvozcuee/mr73ujjix4wnfjs23tyiobc7fy"
TF_VAR_stripe_secret_key_ggg="op://Grove QA/wtfcef4zrfdsvxe3exjnosfigq/guw25u74ogkwtju2evuaykf7hq"
TF_VAR_stripe_secret_key_nursery="op://Grove QA/gi4l6bmv45tyc2uwphutkrd2um/qkd4ehby6hy4np6ymxkssngqqu"

# Webhook signing secrets (GOL-1016). The `webhook_secret` field now exists on
# each stripe-*-qa item (added by Josh 2026-07-31; each length-38, whsec_,
# signature-valid against the real grove_headless verifier). These feed BOTH
# the App Platform storefronts (apps.tf STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET) AND the Odoo
# process env (main.tf -> cloud-init -> compose), where grove_headless's
# handler verifies incoming Stripe-Signature against all three (try-each,
# GOL-1020). op account must be grove-devops-ro / can read Grove QA.
TF_VAR_stripe_webhook_secret_goldberry="op://Grove QA/stripe-goldberry-qa/webhook_secret"
TF_VAR_stripe_webhook_secret_ggg="op://Grove QA/stripe-ggg-qa/webhook_secret"
TF_VAR_stripe_webhook_secret_nursery="op://Grove QA/stripe-nursery-qa/webhook_secret"

# --- Publish-webhook HMAC secrets (GOL-985/986/1004) ------------------------
# Vault `Grove QA`, one item per tenant (grove-publish-webhook-<tenant>-qa),
# field `secret` (openssl rand -hex 32). Kept COMMENTED until the items exist:
# an op:// ref to a missing item is a hard `op run` failure (same reason as
# the stripe webhook secrets above). The ops SA is READ-ONLY on Grove QA, so
# a human with vault WRITE must create these items first (GOL-1004 follow-up).
# goldberry was provisioned LIVE (doctl app env + droplet .env) 2026-07-30 to
# unblock the GOL-1003 E2E; uncomment its ref once the durable item lands, then
# the next `make qa-l3-up` reconciles cleanly. Until then, do NOT re-apply --
# an apply with these commented sets the goldberry secret to "" and 401s the
# live E2E.
#TF_VAR_grove_publish_webhook_secret_goldberry="op://Grove QA/grove-publish-webhook-goldberry-qa/secret"
#TF_VAR_grove_publish_webhook_secret_ggg="op://Grove QA/grove-publish-webhook-ggg-qa/secret"
#TF_VAR_grove_publish_webhook_secret_nursery="op://Grove QA/grove-publish-webhook-nursery-qa/secret"

# --- Ghost Content API keys (prod blogs droplet, read-only) -----------------
# GOL-1013: converged onto the SINGLE JSON-map field prod reads
# (`ghost_content_keys_tf_json` -> TF_VAR_ghost_content_keys), so QA and prod
# share one source of truth and can't drift on key rotation. Same Grove Infra
# item (Goldberry Grove - Admin / uuid qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4). Ref mirrors
# production/.env.op verbatim (name-path, since only the discrete per-blog
# fields had captured UUIDs; the map field's ref matches prod exactly).
# The 4 discrete ghost_content_key_* fields are now unused by any env and a
# HUMAN can delete them from the item once this QA cutover is applied (GOL-1013
# sequencing: cutover FIRST, delete AFTER — vault write needs a human, SA is RO).
TF_VAR_ghost_content_keys=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/ghost_content_keys_tf_json

# Stripe TEST-mode sandbox checkout (GOL-688 / GOL-696 / GOL-899). grove_headless
# reads these as LOWERCASE env (controllers/main.py) — this is the ONLY key the
# checkout SESSION route (/grove/api/v1/checkout/session) reads. All three
# storefronts proxy to it (thin-proxy PRs #278/#279, GOL-890), so an empty value
# here 503s "Checkout is not configured yet" for ggg + goldberry + nursery alike.
# The apply-time `op` account MUST be grove-devops-ro (reads Grove QA + Admin);
# the Admin-only SA resolves Grove QA refs to "" and silently disables checkout.
#   secret_key    → Grove QA vault, item stripe-nursery-qa, field secret_key (below).
#   webhook_secret → whsec_ from the Terra-registered QA endpoint (we_1Tw4NO...),
#     stored on Admin/Grove Infra (grove-qa is read-only to us; can't write it back).
#
# DECISION 2026-07-30 (Josh, GOL-899): use the existing `stripe-nursery-qa` Grove
# QA item as the shared backend key. A prior run commented this out intending to
# mint a dedicated `stripe-odoo-backend-qa` item (scope purity + avoid coupling),
# but that left NO backend key provisioned and silently 503'd checkout for all
# three storefronts once the thin proxies made this env the only path. Josh's
# call: the nursery restricted rk_test_ key is the QA test secret key; its scope
# is empirically sufficient (it creates live Checkout Sessions — GOL-956). Same
# item/field as TF_VAR_stripe_secret_key_nursery above.
#   PROD TODO (do NOT carry this coupling to production): prod must use a
#   DEDICATED backend key, not a storefront key — revoking either must not break
#   the other. Tracked in docs/RUNBOOK-checkout-stripe-guardrails.md.
TF_VAR_stripe_test_secret_key="op://Grove QA/gi4l6bmv45tyc2uwphutkrd2um/qkd4ehby6hy4np6ymxkssngqqu"
TF_VAR_stripe_test_webhook_secret="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/tkgu5xgoc4iidhb42dd6k6ue4m"

# --- Shippo fulfillment (GOL-988 shipping-notification leg) ------------------
# QA uses Shippo TEST-mode credentials from the Grove QA vault item "Shippo Key"
# (created by Josh 2026-08-08): `password` = the test API key (outbound label
# purchase, sale_order.py), `webhook_token` = shared secret for inbound
# tracking-webhook auth (controllers/main.py; the same value must be embedded in
# the webhook URL registered in the Shippo dashboard). Both feed cloud-init
# user_data => first apply REPLACES the QA odoo droplet (filestore volume +
# reserved IP survive, validated GOL-825).
TF_VAR_shippo_api_key="op://Grove QA/Shippo Key/password"
TF_VAR_grove_shippo_webhook_token="op://Grove QA/Shippo Key/webhook_token"

# --- Mailgun SMTP transactional email (GOL-995 / parent GOL-988) -------------
# QA Odoo sends order-confirmation + shipping-notification mail through the hub
# Mailgun sending domain `send.gatheringatthegrove.com` (state=active, SPF+DKIM
# valid). Login `transactional@send.gatheringatthegrove.com` and this password
# live in `Goldberry Grove - Admin` → item `Mailgun | Goldberry Grove` (the op
# service account can read Admin). Ref is UUID+field-id (GOL-394): vault
# 3ajxor4k6iyxapadrxkl6uop3i, item 7t2pap33hu37bftpsy7uzmakuy, field
# smtp_password_hub. UUID form also sidesteps the `|` in the item name, which is
# an invalid character in an op:// name reference. Feeds cloud-init user_data =>
# first apply REPLACES the QA odoo droplet (filestore volume + reserved IP
# survive, validated GOL-825). NOT `mg.*` — that domain is an unmanaged Mailgun
# account; see variables.tf.
TF_VAR_smtp_password="op://3ajxor4k6iyxapadrxkl6uop3i/7t2pap33hu37bftpsy7uzmakuy/kos6jikbzvapkrh3ldlsh3zp6q"
